\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17.3.1}{\ignorespaces The containers that \(Code~\ref {lst:c28-s2l}\) hands upward on \(T\), read bottom-up: e.g.\ \(S_5=S_{\{8\}}\cup \{c_5\}=\{2\}\) (both are colour~2, the set swallows the duplicate), \(S_3=\{1,3\}\) even though five nodes sit below it, and \(S_1=\{1,2,3\}\). The answer vector is the sizes \((3,2,2,1,1,1,2,1,2,1)\) -- note it is \emph  {not} the subtree-size vector \((10,4,5,1,2,1,3,1,2,1)\), which is the other thing these containers are often mistaken for.}}{1039}{figure.caption.182}\protected@file@percent }
